                        "email": "xiazhang@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "seanzhangseu"
                    },
                    "message": "@rashidmp@ami.com Could please share the standard why we need clear the IP addresses when enable DHCP?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Based on my read, this needs reverted.\n\nStatic and DHCP IPs are by design intended to be above to be set at the same time.  This facilitates some testing and mixed-dynamic-static use cases.  Functionally, clearing all static IPs when DHCP is enabled would break Redfish EthernetInterface functionality which treats them as separate.\n\n@raviteja28031990@gmail.com @rashidmp@ami.com does the above make sense to you?  Can we fix this please?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, we can revert this commit for now\n@rashidmp@ami.com can you please revert this commit"
                },
